  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- The internal build (`Intrada.Alpr.Internal`) adds `IIntradaAlpr.IsTypeCodeEnabled`, which tells whether Intrada reports plate type codes.\n- Intrada.NET runs on macOS. It loads `libintrada.dylib`, and Intrada loads its country modules as `libintrada_cm_*.so`.\n- When `IntradaOptions.Path` is not set, the Intrada library is looked for in the `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` (Linux) or `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` (macOS) directories first, then in the application's directory. On Linux, a `libintrada.so` on `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` is now loaded instead of one next to the application.\n- The working directory is no longer searched for the Intrada library, so a library placed there cannot be loaded in place of yours. Set `IntradaOptions.Path`, or place Intrada next to your application.\n- With `IntradaOptions.Path` not set, Intrada 7.10 and later look for country modules in the `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` (Linux) or `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` (macOS) directories before the directory of the Intrada library, and read `intrada.lic`, `intrada_env.txt`, `intrada_logsettings.txt` and `intrada.pvm` from the working directory when they are not in the directory of the library. With `Path` set, or with earlier versions, all of these come from the directory of the library.",
  "verbatimVersion": "7.10.0",
